====== TP-Link TD-W9980 / TD-W9980B ======
The TD-W9980 is a VDSL-capable router launched in 2014. It's identical to the [[td-w8980_v1|TD-W8980]], so check that page out as some information is there and some here. The device works very well with OpenWrt, including the integrated DSL modem. Just the 5 GHz Wifi cannot be used and for VDSL you'll need to use a propriertary binary blob as described in this article.

This page is also for **TD-W9980B** which is nearly identical, with the exception that you can't flash via the Web UI exploit.

:!: The **B** is for annex B and [[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/td-w9980b-dsl-pppoe-error-network-device-is-not-present/62948/6?u=f00wl|cannot be changed]]. Check if your provider use this [[wp>G.992.3#ADSL2_Annexes|annex]]


OEM source code available at: [[http://static.tp-link.com/resources/gpl/GPL_TD-W9980.tar.gz|GPL_TD-W9980.tar.gz]]

